<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</title>
<headline>Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping sugar.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: Karyatis III loading 25,000 tonnes using big bags.</p>
<p>Waiting to dock, nine vessels to load using big bags and one bulk.</p>
<p>Road: 235 trucks carrying sugar arrived between June 6 and 8.</p>
<p>Loading: no figures available.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: Araya loading 35,200 tonnes bulk sugar, Cormorant loading 14,000 tonnes bagged sugar, Unisea loading 14,000 tonnes bagged sugar, Qing Jiang loading 14,000 bagged sugar. Waiting to dock, six vessels to load bagged sugar and two to load bulk.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
